        "_key": "a2-1",
        "_type": "tldrBox",
        "items": [
          "For most UK SMBs with 5–15 pages, a **custom-coded website** beats WordPress on speed, SEO and long-term value.",
          "**WordPress wins** if you publish 10+ articles a month, need daily self-editing, or run a large catalogue.",
          "**Custom wins** if speed matters (Lighthouse 95+), you want no lock-in, you need integrations, or SEO matters from day one.",
          "The number that decides it is **3-year total cost of ownership**, not the upfront build."
        ],
        "title": "In 60 seconds"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-3",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-2",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "What is a custom-coded website?"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-5",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-4",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "A custom website is built from scratch, with no theme and no page builder. We write the front end in Next.js and run the content through Sanity, so every line of code exists because your site needs it, not because a template shipped with it. Nothing loads that you didn’t ask for."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-a",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-6",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "That control is what produces the speed. "
          },
          {
            "_key": "a2-8",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [
              "a2-7"
            ],
            "text": "Efedra Clinic"
          },
          {
            "_key": "a2-9",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": ", one of our builds, holds a Lighthouse score of 98 and a largest-contentful-paint of 0.8 seconds. You don’t reach those numbers by bolting a caching plugin onto a theme; you reach them by not shipping the bloat in the first place."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-7",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "/en/portfolio/efedra-clinic",
            "newTab": false
          }
        ],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-c",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-b",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "What is WordPress?"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-e",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-d",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "WordPress is a PHP content management system that powers roughly 43% of the web. You pick a theme, add plugins for the features you need, and edit through a dashboard most people already recognise. That ecosystem is its strength: there is a plugin for almost anything, and developers are easy to find."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-g",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-f",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "The cost of that flexibility is weight and upkeep. Every plugin is more code to load, another thing to update, and another possible security hole. None of that makes WordPress bad. It makes it a particular set of trade-offs."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
      },
      {
        "_key": "a2-i",
        "_type": "block",
        "children": [
          {
            "_key": "a2-h",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "Side-by-side comparison"
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "h2"
      },
